@startuml
' Figure 7.6 – System sequence diagram: the voice round trip
' Sprint 8 (FR-82, FR-83). Sources: src/ai/voice.service.ts,
' src/ai/voice-billing.ts and the transcribe/speak routes in ai.controller.ts;
' features/ai/use-voice-input.ts and use-speech-out.ts (frontend).
!include ../_style.puml
mainframe interaction SequenceDiagram Voice round trip
autonumber "0 :"

participant "Writer" as R
participant "Assistant\npanel" as P
participant "System" as A
participant "Speech-to-text\n(Groq Whisper)" as S
participant "Text-to-speech\n(Gemini)" as T
participant "Database" as D

ref over R, D : Sign in

R -> P : Record a prompt (at most 5 minutes)
activate P
P -> A : POST /ai/transcribe with the audio and its length
activate A
A -> A : Check the allowance, the audio type and the size

alt longer than 5 minutes, or over the byte cap
  A --> P : 413, "Recording too long (max 5 minutes)"
else accepted
  A -> S : Transcribe
  activate S
  S --> A : Text and, when reported, its duration
  deactivate S
  A -> A : Seconds = the provider's duration, else the larger of the\nclient's figure and a floor derived from the bytes, capped at 300
  A -> D : Bill 200 tokens per started minute, one minute at least
  activate D
  D --> A : New balance
  deactivate D
  A --> P : Text, seconds and tokens used
  deactivate A
  P --> R : The transcript in the composer, editable
end

R -> P : Send the brief
ref over P, D : Assistant turn (figure 7.4)

opt the key can speak, and the writer has not muted
  P -> A : POST /ai/speak with the reply's text
  activate A
  A -> A : Check 20 a minute and 300 a day for this account
  A -> T : Synthesise the text
  activate T
  T --> A : Audio
  deactivate T
  A --> P : WAV, not billed
  deactivate A
  P --> R : Play the reply
end
deactivate P

note over R, D
  Dictation costs tokens; listening does not. Reading aloud is rate-limited
  per account instead, and the mute control exists only when
  GET /ai/speech-availability says the key can speak. The mute choice
  persists in the browser.
end note
@enduml
